      "message": "Got it. Added the check for single quotes. \n\nBTW, I found a valid case where space don\u0027t need to be wrapped in quotes.\n\n\"-DADD(x, y)\u003d((x) + (y))\"\n\nthough defining a function macro here is absolute not a good practice, I can\u0027t find a good \nreason to reject it here.",
