      "writtenOn": "2017-09-27T22:58:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s actually bringing up a real issue.  There isn\u0027t actually any need for quotes - if Soong sees a space in the cflag it is going to quote the entire cflag in single quotes, which will make it into a single argument on the command line.  The quotes will be passed through and turn the macro contents into a string literal, which may not always be desired.\n\nIf you put multiple cflags into one clang is likely to to show \"unknown warning option: \u0027-Wall -Wnone\u0027.  I think we should just simplify this to allow spaces if the argument starts with -D.",
      "parentUuid": "17578a60_7b1bc8d8",
      "revId": "9fa0549b25c9be30d2e9cd0024511b8312f0c534",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
